guide forever/professions/mining
title Mining 1-300
category Professions
coords era
levels 1-60
zone Ironforge

# Mining 1-300 for both factions: for each skill band, a loop the arrow walks
# through the densest ground of nodes the skill can mine (expected skill-ups per
# yard of a lap, with the time to mine each node and the nodes' respawn), at
# the lowest character level that keeps the loop nearly as good: no creature on
# it more than a level above that level, and away from the other faction's
# towns. Nodes are the Forever server's own spawns with the chance its spawn
# pools keep each up, and what a node gives comes from players' recorded
# gathers (tools/lib/professions/gathering/gathering-nodes.json).
# Skill needed per node: Copper 1, Tin and Incendicite 65, Silver and Lesser
# Bloodstone 75, Iron 125, Gold 155, Mithril 175, Truesilver and Dark Iron 230,
# Small Thorium 245, Rich Thorium 275.
#
# Herb and ore spawns come from the Forever TrinityCore world DB (its spawn pools
# say how often each is up); beast spawns and levels from the reference data;
# trainer learn skills and prices from Forever's sniffed trainer lists; recipes
# and their skill colours from the Forever client tables.
# Zones are ranked for a character of a fifth of the band's skill in levels (at
# least 5; ASSUMED: one levelling with the profession); a loop that asks more
# says so with a `level` goal, and loses half its worth per level it asks above.
# Ranks ask no character level: Forever's sniffed trainer lists carry none for
# Herbalism, Mining or Skinning, and players' recordings show Expert Mining
# trained at 15 and Artisan Skinning at 29.
# Waypoints are Era-frame (`coords era`); the engine converts them where Forever
# changed a map frame, and a map without an Era frame (Zephras Isle) compiles live.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Apprentice
section Mining 1-65

step Learn Mining
  tip Any Mining trainer of your faction teaches Apprentice Mining at any level (10c), and so does the Junior Mining Trainer in each starting area; the arrow picks the nearest. Buy a Mining Pick from a trade goods or general vendor: keep it in your bags, you cannot mine without it. Turn on Find Minerals (spellbook, General tab) so veins show on the minimap. Forever's starting areas also have Poor Copper Veins (Copper Ore and Rough Stone, from skill 1). The first-hour quest of each starting area (Rascally Rodents, Coldridge Valley Mail Delivery, The Woodland Protector, Galgar's Cactus Apple Surprise, A Humble Task, Marla's Last Wish) offers Mining for Dummies as a reward: reading it gives 2 skill, up to 15. Trade goods vendors and the junior trainers sell the Apprentice's Mining Pack, a four-slot bag for ore and stone (25c). If you sat at your starting area's campfire for The Great Outdoors, the camping guide there also offers Camping 101: Mining: hand it in to the mining trainer it names once you reach skill 20, for the Lodestone recipe.
  train Mining Apprentice
  buy 2901 x1 nearest

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mining 1-65

step Chunk of Amber & Poor Copper (1-50)
  tip Walk the loop and mine every Chunk of Amber (1, orange), Copper (1, orange), Large Chunk of Amber (1, orange), Poor Copper (1, orange) node on the way until Mining 50. Smelt at a forge when your bags fill: Smelt Copper (orange to 25, grey at 70) gives points too. The arrow takes the loop that gets you there soonest from where you are and walks it until the skill is reached; each loop keeps to creatures no more than a level above you and away from the other faction's towns, and the window names it and its lap. Expect about 60 nodes for these 49 points: about 55 Copper Ore and 55 Rough Stone. For Blacksmithing: about 485 Copper Ore and 195 Rough Stone in all. For Engineering: about 260 Copper Ore and 35 Rough Stone in all.
