# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Mining 65-125
section Mining 65-125

step Smelt Bronze & Smelt Tin
  tip At 65 a Mining trainer teaches Smelt Bronze (2s; grey at 115) and Smelt Tin (50c; grey at 75): smelting at a forge raises Mining too, so smelt what you mine.
  learn 2659
  learn 3304

step Tin (65-125)
  tip Walk the loop and mine every Copper (1, green), Incendicite (65, orange), Tin (65, orange) node on the way until Mining 125. Smelt at a forge when your bags fill: Smelt Copper (orange to 25, grey at 70), Smelt Tin (grey at 75), Smelt Bronze (grey at 115) give points too. Smelt Bronze takes a Copper Bar and a Tin Bar each: keep bars from the smelts before it. A quest in these zones needs Mining: Ingredients for the Forge (level 30, Morhan Coppertongue, Loch Modan; Alliance). The arrow takes the loop that gets you there soonest from where you are and walks it until the skill is reached; each loop keeps to creatures no more than a level above you and away from the other faction's towns, and the window names it and its lap. Expect about 160 nodes for these 60 points: about 80 Copper Ore, 65 Tin Ore, 55 Rough Stone, 40 Coarse Stone, 15 Blood Shard, 10 Incendicite Ore and 5 Pyrite. For Blacksmithing: about 485 Copper Ore, 165 Tin Ore, 195 Rough Stone and 100 Coarse Stone in all. For Engineering: about 260 Copper Ore, 95 Tin Ore, 35 Rough Stone and 45 Coarse Stone in all. Smelt Silver (2s; orange to 100, grey at 125) is taught from 75: learn it if you pass a Mining trainer, it is not worth a trip of its own.
